// Environment assumptions. An "assumption" is not a special node kind or keyword —
// it is just a proposition discharged in fiat mode (concept §2.1). Parents reference
// these through ordinary children; DAG sharing covers reuse.
//
// The ID'd shared-definition "registry" (concept §6.4) is a veriq-integration
// mechanism (M8): calcs declare assumes=["<id>"] and the aggregated assumption set
// presented at bind approval needs identity-based aggregation. It never appears in
// argument-side syntax.

fiat approvers_follow_norm {
  ```
  Approvers follow the norm: when a judgement required reading the subtree, either decline, or demand a revision that promotes what was learned into the children's contracts
  ```
}

fiat git_hosting_intact {
  ```
  The repository hosting infrastructure (git history and the CI execution environment) is not controlled by an attacker
  ```
}